\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 BUGS/ISSUES:
\f1\b0\fs26 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Every jump/goto executes the last half of the dress a a command\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li1440\fi-1440\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}This is because the jump command doesn\'92t skip the MSB of the jump address, making the computer see it as a command. Currently no successful workaround, trying a few ideas though\
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Commands mislabeled\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li1440\fi-1440\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Some commands I have added to my computer are currently mislabeled or not functioning like it was described in the documentation. Since there aren\'92t that many commands to try, and if one alternative works you can extrapolate the rest, its relatively easy to correct all commands\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}There are some commands I still need to add though. For instance, the 16 Bit variety of inc and move are not implemented and some new commands are also not finished, such as HALT or the IN command.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Bus weirdness >:(\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li1440\fi-1440\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}The buses of my system are somewhat wonky and make, at times, zero sense. For example, the increment function of the ALU gave back results with the MSB and LSB swapped, so that 00000001 became 10000000. This is very not good.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}The somewhat standard components I used for this computer are somewhat cool, the problem arises when you to change one single thing, and now the whole system just doesn\'92t work anymore. I have two solutions for this problem:\
\pard\tx1660\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li2160\fi-2160\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl2\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}The first option would be to make the separate components less standard. The issue with that would be that if you have an issue with the system, it would be less straightforward to troubleshoot the system.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}The second, and my preferred option, would be to make bigger compartments, where, for example, all registers would have one block, the ALU would have one block and the other operational logic would have one block. This could also make it harder to troubleshoot, but could make the design also a bit more modular, since you could just add more logic if you need to. Without making the system more cluttered.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Simplification\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li1440\fi-1440\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}The next thing to do after most of the bugs and weirdness is found, is to simplify the design and reduce the chip count in general. We are currently sitting at a cool ~430 separate chips. This is a really big amount of chips, way more than I anticipated. Not only would this make me go broke at the moment, but it would most likely use a LOT of power, let\'92s quickly do some napkin math:\
\pard\tx1660\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li2160\fi-2160\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl2\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Buffers tend to use around 240 to 300 mW each\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Quad-Gate chips such as a 74LS00 use around 9 to 22 mW \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Since I want to use a SRAM chip so I don\'92t have to build a refresh circuit, it would consume around 200 to 400 mW\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}We have 132 Buffers, 250 Gates, and a few miscellaneous chips such as counters\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}If we were to assume the worst possible situation, we would have a consumption of\'85 around 45 W of power!\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}Since this computer primarily runs on 5 Volts, this would equate to an amperage of 9 amps.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li1440\fi-1440\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}This is of course the worst possible outcome of all chips having 100% utility, which is highly unlikely. The consumption will probably not even be half of the worst case. The only thing I could see becoming an issue would be the heat produced by so many chips.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}\
